  "defence": {
    "_source": "Carlos Oct 15 playtest: switching, tackle, compact defence; numbers PROPOSAL. Defending with the ball in its own half (blended in over blendMetres behind compactFromX), the back line holds one line lineBehindBall metres behind the ball (never deeper than deepestLine), the midfield line lineGap in front; width = base width x compactWidth shifted ballSideShift x the ball's distance from the middle. The nearest player presses, the next covers; up to markRunners of the most dangerous runners (in the box, at or behind the line within behindLineMargin, or running at goal faster than runnerSpeed within runnerZone of the line; order: nearest the goal, +boxBonus in the box, +runnerBonus for runners) are man-marked by the nearest free defender or midfielder within pickupRadius; defenders add deepRunnerBias for a runner more than deepRunnerGap in front of the line, so midfielders track runners from deep. Markers aim markLeadSeconds ahead of the runner and sprint beyond markSprintDistance. Targets: block (defenders + midfielders) at most 30 m deep and 45 m wide with the ball in its own third.",
